Implement pathfinding around units for cases where local separation alone cannot
make progress.

Use a lightweight dynamic-obstacle approach appropriate for this open 120x120
battlefield. A coarse A* grid with cached paths is acceptable. Direct movement
should remain the normal fast path; pathfinding should activate only when the
direct corridor is obstructed or a unit has failed to make meaningful progress
for the configured blocked-time threshold.

Requirements:

1. Store per-unit navigation state separately from strategic target_pos:
   - final destination;
   - current path waypoints;
   - current waypoint index;
   - blocked/progress timer;
   - last path calculation time;
   - enough destination information to detect stale paths.

2. Build dynamic occupancy from living units:
   - inflate occupied cells by unit radius minus allowed soft overlap;
   - allow the mover's own cell;
   - do not make the exact final target permanently unreachable;
   - handle a combat target specially so melee units can approach attack range
     rather than trying to occupy the target's center;
   - allow limited passage through moving allies when necessary, but strongly
     prefer open cells;
   - treat stationary kings and guards as strong obstacles unless they are the
     intended combat target.

3. Before A*, check whether the direct corridor is clear.
4. Use deterministic A* tie-breaking.
5. Permit diagonal movement only if it cannot cut through blocked corners.
6. Convert the cell path to world-space waypoints and simplify it with
   line-of-sight checks.
7. Recalculate paths only when:
   - the destination changes materially;
   - the next corridor becomes blocked;
   - progress remains insufficient;
   - the refresh interval expires.
8. Clear navigation state when orders are cancelled, targets die, units die, or
   a destination is reached.
9. Clamp every waypoint and resulting position to map bounds.
10. If no route currently exists, keep the order alive and retry later instead
    of deleting it.

Add tests for:
- walking around a stationary wall of units;
- navigating a narrow but valid gap;
- not cutting diagonally through blocked corners;
- approaching an enemy only to attack range;
- replanning when a blocker moves into the path;
- reusing a cached path when nothing changes;
- recovering when a temporary route is unavailable;
- replacing a path when the player issues a new order;
- deterministic paths across repeated runs;
- destinations near all four map edges.

Checks:
- Run the focused pathfinding tests.
- Run the complete test suite.
- Instrument path-calculation counts in tests and confirm paths are not
  recalculated every frame.
- Report the worst path length and recalculation count in the test scenarios.
- Do not commit changes.
